{
  "id": "chrome",
  "name": "Google Chrome",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Browser",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "chrome.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.google.Chrome"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/157179"
  ],
  "note": "From Google's \"Chrome keyboard shortcuts\" support page (Windows/Linux and Mac tabs). Where the vendor lists multiple alternate chords for one action (e.g. \"Ctrl+W or Ctrl+F4\"), only the primary chord is recorded, since one action carries one chord per platform. \"Ctrl+1 through Ctrl+8\" is expanded into 8 explicit tab-jump actions. Skipped as not expressible: all Mouse-shortcut entries (drag-and-drop, click/right-click combinations, mouse-wheel zoom/scroll) and the Fn-key-dependent Mac full-screen shortcut (Fn+F).",
  "actions": [
    {
      "name": "Open a new window",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Ctrl+N"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Cmd+N"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Open a new window in Incognito mode",
      "context": "",
      "windows": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Ctrl+Shift+N"
      },
      "mac": {
        "type": "keys",
        "chord": "Cmd+Shift+N"
      }
    },
